{
  "summary": "This experiment tested an image-only model using ResNet50 encoder with singleprofile settings, achieving low validation accuracy (0.208) and F1 (0.172). The results suggest image modality alone may not contribute meaningfully to performance in this setting, but uncertainty remains about optimal image processing techniques or potential interactions with other modalities. The stark underperformance relative to RNA-only baselines (e.g., 0.485 accuracy) highlights the need to explore more effective image encoders or multimodal integration strategies."
}

